<%- include('partials/header') %>

<h2>ZKP (Selective Disclosure) Demo</h2>
<p>This is a UI-level demo that simulates selective disclosure without revealing full credential details.</p>

<div class="card p-3">
  <p><strong>Scenario:</strong> Employer only wants to know whether candidate has a B.Tech degree and is older than 18.</p>
  <p><strong>Action:</strong> Student clicks <em>Show Proof</em> — the system reveals boolean proofs only.</p>

  <div class="mt-3">
    <button id="showProof" class="btn btn-primary">Show Proof</button>
  </div>

  <div id="proofArea" class="mt-3" style="display:none;">
    <div class="alert alert-success"><strong>Degree Verified:</strong> true</div>
    <div class="alert alert-success"><strong>Age &gt;= 18:</strong> true</div>
    <div class="alert alert-info">Note: No marks, university ID or full certificate image revealed.</div>
  </div>
</div>

<script>
  document.getElementById('showProof').addEventListener('click', () => {
    document.getElementById('proofArea').style.display = 'block';
  });
</script>

